{
 "about": [
  "What each session is and where the lists show it (PROTOCOL.md, \"Session lists\"): `kuvo/sessions/list`'s facts from a box's engine sessions,",
  "and the sidebar a client draws from them. `box` is what the box knows beside its sessions: its chats and bots folders, its bots' conversations,",
  "the project each folder is filed under (`worktrees` of `kuvo/projects`), its project list, those at work, since when each waits on you (by the",
  "conversation, a subagent's ask counting as its own), and the copies that aren't its own. `expect.sessions` and `expect.projects` are the box's",
  "answer (box/test/session-lists.test.ts checks them); `expect.sidebar` is what a client shows from them (KuvoClient's SessionListsTests):",
  "pinned and chats newest first; projects by their newest session shown, ties by name (Finder order: case-insensitive, numbers by value), the",
  "name its list gives else its folder's last part; sessions in a project newest first. Written by hand from the Mac's rule as it was before",
  "the box said it (Workspace.makeProjects, 2026-11-13); change both together.",
  "`box.asks` is what each one waiting asks, in the box's words, and `box.botOf` the bot each bot's conversation is; `expect.needsYou` is the",
  "list's \"Needs you\" (the one that asked last first), `expect.projects[].asking`/`working` each project's sums (one asking isn't counted at work),",
  "and `expect.bots` what each bot is doing now (`now` in `kuvo/bots`), all from the facts (#711).",
  "Since `bots.state`: `box.thinking` those whose model has been reasoning a while, `box.stopped` each one that stopped on an error or a limit and",
  "hasn't run since (`by`, and `idle`, the turn it stopped, where the box knows it), `box.retrying` what each one retrying a while retries; thinking",
  "and retrying count only while it's at work (one blocked by a retry says `retrying`). A session's `unread` is its `time.idle` while that's later than `time.viewed`; a stop blocks it only",
  "while that turn is unread. `expect.bots` adds how many of those at work think, how many are blocked and by what (the newest), and `unseen`, the",
  "newest turn not read of those neither at work, asking nor blocked, which its state comes from."
 ],
